        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Durable Core PR 4/6: persist agent-turn front doors",
        "body": "## Stack Position\n\nDurable Core PR 4/6, gated on the latest completed ClawSweeper review for PR3 #111278 (overall Gold Shrimp).\n\nThis PR targets `release/2026.7.1`, so GitHub shows the cumulative durable-core stack. The reviewable PR4-only delta is:\n\nhttps://github.com/mjnkao/openclaw/compare/codex/durable-core-pr3-recovery-v5...codex/durable-core-pr4-agent-turn-v1\n\n- Stack parent: `3c344e0a98f34dbb954275f45ca738f744aea3e7`\n- Exact head: `2e95463c53aa4bd025c7702634dab684d209b85c`\n- Database schema delta from PR3: none\n- New configuration delta from PR3: none\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw 7.1 entry points can acknowledge agent work before durable evidence exists. During long tool work, Gateway restart can leave the caller with an uncertain outcome; the established CLI fallback or restart recovery can then run the same work again and risk duplicate side effects.\n\nThis slice persists admission, liveness, and settlement around existing agent-turn and `chat.send` front doors:\n\n- channel reply and queued follow-up runners\n- CLI Gateway path\n- isolated cron execution\n- Gateway `agent` RPC\n- OpenAI-compatible HTTP streaming\n- OpenResponses streaming\n- `chat.send`\n\nIt reuses the PR2 durable tables and PR3 recovery/owner-attention substrate. It adds no generic executor, parallel worker, database table, or hidden environment activation path.\n\n## Contract\n\n- Persist intake before dispatch or success-shaped acceptance output.\n- Await durable admission before the first OpenAI assistant chunk.\n- Await durable admission before OpenResponses created/in-progress/output events.\n- Fail closed in `authority` mode when intake cannot be persisted.\n- Keep `observe` best effort and disabled mode database-free.\n- Renew a 30-second heartbeat while a turn is active.\n- Settle each turn through one fenced terminal path.\n- Store message length and SHA-256 hash, not raw prompt text.\n- Mark intake metadata-only and non-replayable.\n- Refuse CLI embedded fallback after an uncertain Gateway result.\n- Block main-session auto-resume while an open `lost_after_dispatch` fact exists.\n- Deliver restart attention with tools disabled, including after persistent queue recovery.\n- Keep explicit retry authority with the source owner.\n\n## Current-Head Corrections\n\nClawSweeper's previous review found that both HTTP streaming paths could emit success-shaped events before asynchronous durable admission rejected. Exact head `235f75d` introduced one awaitable ingress admission boundary, preserved the same run identity and lifecycle generation, and added rejection regressions for both endpoints.\n\nLive fault validation then found a second replay route: the durable restart wake could activate the interrupted transcript and the model could repeat a missing tool process despite the warning prompt. Exact head `2e95463` closes that route at deterministic owner boundaries:\n\n1. Main-session restart recovery performs a read-only authority-mode uncertainty check and will not auto-resume a transcript with open side-effect uncertainty.\n2. A `restart_interrupted` attention payload persists `disableTools=true`; queue recovery preserves it and the heartbeat runner removes all tools and skills for that attention turn.\n3. Durable attention is classified as a real wake payload, so an empty `HEARTBEAT.md` cannot suppress the owner update.\n\nThe replay fence is independent of model strength, prompt compliance, or context-window size.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Exact-head validation\n\nExact head `2e95463c53aa4bd025c7702634dab684d209b85c` passed:\n\n- focused current-head matrix: 359 tests across 5 Vitest shards\n- unit shard: 32 passed\n- Gateway OpenAI/OpenResponses matrix: 159 passed\n- infra heartbeat/system-event/session-queue shard: 96 passed\n- command/fail-closed fallback shard: 37 passed\n- main-session restart-recovery shard: 35 passed\n- `pnpm tsgo:all`\n- changed-file type-aware Oxlint\n- `pnpm lint:agent:ingress-owner`\n- Oxfmt on all changed files\n- `git diff --check`\n- exact-head `pnpm build`, reporting `OpenClaw 2026.7.1 (2e95463)`\n\nRegression coverage proves:\n\n- OpenAI admission failure emits no assistant success chunk.\n- OpenResponses admission failure emits no created, in-progress, or output event.\n- Open durable side-effect uncertainty blocks main-session auto-resume.\n- Restart attention preserves `disableTools=true` through the persistent queue.\n- Durable attention bypasses an empty heartbeat file without exposing tools.\n\n### Exact-head isolated restart and no-replay trace\n\nAn isolated authority-mode Gateway used channels/bindings disabled and a private loopback endpoint.\n\n1. A normal CLI-to-Gateway turn persisted `received -> running -> succeeded`.\n2. A second turn appended one line to an isolated side-effect counter, then entered a 120-second tool wait.\n3. Before shutdown it remained `running/running`, recorded a heartbeat at 30,002 ms, and the side-effect count was exactly one.\n4. Gateway shutdown made the waiting CLI exit non-zero with the explicit uncertain-outcome message; embedded fallback did not run.\n5. Restart against the same SQLite state produced exactly one `lost/lost` turn, one open `lost_after_dispatch` fact, and one `restart_interrupted` wake.\n6. The attached attention turn ran without tools and ACKed the wake in one attempt.\n7. The side-effect count remained one and the transcript contained exactly one `exec` call and zero `process` calls.\n8. A separate post-restart CLI turn succeeded normally.\n9. A third boot changed only the Gateway startup count.\n\nStable counts across the third boot:\n\n```text\nlost_agent_turns=1\nsucceeded_agent_turns=3\nuncertainty_facts=1\nopen_uncertainty_facts=1\nwake_obligations=1\nacked_wakes=1\nwake_attempts=1\nside_effect_count=1\ntranscript_exec_calls=1\n```\n\nThe isolated durable database contained zero raw proof-marker occurrences in `metadata_json`; records retained bounded lengths and hashes only.\n\n## Boundary\n\nThis PR does not claim arbitrary tool-process resumption, automatic replay from metadata-only intake, exactly-once external effects, or external-channel delivery. Durable core records uncertain effects, prevents automatic replay, and routes owner attention; reconciliation or explicit retry remains an owner decision.\n\nPR5 remains the subagent lifecycle/restart bridge. PR6 remains the read-only operational API/CLI surface.\n\nThis PR is AI-assisted. The implementation and proof were manually reviewed against the owner-authority, admission, recovery, replay, privacy, and disabled-mode boundaries above.",
